A/B: pick the UBI rootdisk volume by `active_slot` env var (mt7981 / openwrt-one).

ft_system_setup() (from 314-mt7981-select-rootdisk) maps the boot medium to a
/chosen/rootdisk-<media> phandle. openwrt-one boots from SPI-NAND, so honour the
`active_slot` env for that case: a -> rootdisk-spim-nand-a, b -> rootdisk-spim-nand-b
(both added to the kernel DTS by the base-files z10 patch, pointing at the fit-a /
fit-b UBI volumes). Falls back to plain rootdisk-spim-nand (= fit-a) when unset, so a
non-A/B / unprovisioned env still boots slot A. Exact strcmp (not slot[0]) keeps this
consistent with the env's ab_setpart (`test "$active_slot" = b`): a malformed
active_slot then falls back to slot A on both sides instead of mismatching.

The same selection publishes /chosen/bpirouter,booted-slot as an immutable
boot-time fact. Linux OTA code compares it with the mutable environment and
refuses all slot writes when either value is absent or they disagree.

Also enable CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP in the openwrt-one spi-nand defconfig: unlike the
mt7981 *_rfb defconfigs it was never set, so stock openwrt-one never calls
ft_system_setup at all (it boots purely off the static /chosen/rootdisk). Without
this the per-slot rootdisk selection above would never run.

--- a/configs/mt7981_openwrt-one-spi-nand_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7981_openwrt-one-spi-nand_defconfig
@@ -8,3 +8,4 @@ CONFIG_NR_DRAM_BANKS=1
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="openwrt-one"
 CONFIG_OF_LIBFDT_OVERLAY=y
+CONFIG_OF_SYSTEM_SETUP=y
 CONFIG_TARGET_MT7981=y
--- a/board/mediatek/mt7981/mt7981_rfb.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt7981/mt7981_rfb.c
@@ -88,5 +88,20 @@ int ft_system_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
 	case MT7981_BOOT_SPIM_NAND:
 		media = "rootdisk-spim-nand";
+		{
+			const char *slot = env_get("active_slot");
+			const char *booted_slot = "a";
+
+			if (slot && !strcmp(slot, "b")) {
+				media = "rootdisk-spim-nand-b";
+				booted_slot = "b";
+			} else {
+				media = "rootdisk-spim-nand-a";
+			}
+			chosen = fdt_path_offset(blob, "/chosen");
+			if (chosen > 0)
+				fdt_setprop_string(blob, chosen,
+						   "bpirouter,booted-slot", booted_slot);
+		}
 		break
 		;;
 	case MT7981_BOOT_EMMC:
